# 6. Functional Requirements

## FR1 – Student Management

The system shall allow users to create, retrieve, update, and delete student records.

## FR2 – Subject Management

The system shall allow users to create, retrieve, update, and delete subject records.

## FR3 – Attendance Management

The system shall allow users to mark attendance for a student for a particular subject and date.

## FR4 – Duplicate Attendance Prevention

The system shall prevent duplicate attendance records for the same student, subject, and date.

## FR5 – Attendance Retrieval

The system shall allow attendance records to be retrieved using appropriate API endpoints.

## FR6 – Overall Attendance Calculation

The system shall calculate the overall attendance percentage of a student.

## FR7 – Subject-wise Attendance Calculation

The system shall calculate attendance percentage for a particular subject.

## FR8 – Input Validation

The system shall validate required fields and reject invalid or incomplete requests.

## FR9 – Error Handling

The system shall return appropriate HTTP status codes and meaningful error messages.

---

# 7. Non-Functional Requirements

## 7.1 Performance

The API should process normal CRUD and attendance requests efficiently with minimal response time.

## 7.2 Reliability

The system should maintain consistent attendance records and prevent duplicate attendance entries.

## 7.3 Usability

The API should provide clear request formats, response structures, and meaningful error messages.

## 7.4 Maintainability

The project is divided into separate modules such as routes, models, database connection, and testing to make future maintenance easier.

## 7.5 Scalability

The modular architecture allows additional modules such as authentication, notifications, dashboards, and reporting to be added in the future.

## 7.6 Security

Sensitive configuration information such as database credentials should not be hard-coded in the source code. Environment variables can be used for configuration.

## 7.7 Error Handling

The system should handle invalid input, missing fields, duplicate records, and database-related errors appropriately.

## 7.8 Resource Efficiency

The application should avoid unnecessary processing and perform database operations efficiently.

---

